Independent implementation
--------------------------
OpenShape is an independent, clean-room implementation of a parametric CAD
system. It contains no code, file formats, icons, artwork or other assets
of any proprietary CAD product. Its feature goals are benchmarked against
commercial CAD systems, including Onshape. Onshape is a trademark of PTC
Inc. OpenShape is not affiliated with, endorsed by or derived from PTC Inc.
or its products. The policy, and the public sources OpenShape relies on, are
in docs/CLEANROOM.md.

Every icon in OpenShape is an original drawing made for it, in code
(crates/ui-kit/src/icons.rs).

Third-party components
----------------------
OpenShape links third-party Rust crates from crates.io, listed with their
exact versions in Cargo.lock. Each is under a licence compatible with
GPL-3.0-or-later, checked on every build by cargo-deny (deny.toml); their
licence texts are in the crates' own source distributions.

The user interface draws text with the fonts bundled by the egui toolkit
(crate epaint_default_fonts):
  - Ubuntu Light: Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0
  - Hack: MIT License, with the Bitstream Vera License for the glyphs from
    Bitstream Vera Sans Mono (the DejaVu contributions are public domain)
  - Noto Emoji: SIL Open Font License 1.1
  - emoji-icon-font (John Slegers): MIT License

Sketch text is laid out in fonts bundled with OpenShape (crates/text/fonts),
unmodified:
  - Liberation Sans, Liberation Serif and Liberation Mono 2.1.5, regular
    and bold: SIL Open Font License 1.1. Digitized data copyright (c) 2010
    Google Corporation, with Reserved Font Arimo, Tinos and Cousine;
    copyright (c) 2012 Red Hat, Inc., with Reserved Font Name Liberation.
    The licence and notices are in crates/text/fonts/OFL.txt.
Text is shaped with the harfrust crate (MIT License), the HarfBuzz
project's Rust port of its shaping algorithm, and font metrics and glyph
outlines are read with the skrifa and read-fonts crates (MIT OR
Apache-2.0) of the fontations project.
